    {
      "id": "ES-C55-sintesis-preterito-completo",
      "sequence": 2260,
      "title": "Synthesis — telling what happened",
      "headword": "telling what happened",
      "romanization": "telling what happened",
      "gloss": "a past you can tell about other people — and the form the next chapter is built from",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:91bea38868b83f00",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Hablaron. Fueron. Two plurals, two different bargains — one regular, one refusing every ending in the language."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three chapters ago your past tense could still only talk about one person at a time. Now it can talk about a group:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                ""
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 4,
              "utterances": [
                "Hablaron español., They spoke Spanish.",
                "Comimos en casa., We ate at home.",
                "Tuvieron tiempo., They had time.",
                "Fueron profesores., They were teachers."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That is the difference between keeping a diary and telling a story. A story needs other people in it, and other people need a plural."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: the form that pays twice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One of the five forms you just learned is about to do a second job."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "hablaron, comieron, tuvieron, fueron."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Swap the -ron for -ra and something appears that Spanish uses for supposing: hablara, comiera, tuviera, fuera. That is the form the next chapters need — the one that lets you say if I had time rather than if I have time."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You are not learning it yet. You are being told that you already own the raw material, which is why the plural had to come first."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "Hablaron español y tuvieron tiempo",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *Hablaron español y tuvieron tiempo*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "Fueron profesores",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *Fueron profesores*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "repeat",
              "times": 2,
              "source": "[REPEAT x2]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C55-sintesis-preterito-completo-story",
              "prompt": "Say: they spoke Spanish and they had time.",
              "assesses": [
                "ES-GRAMMAR-AR-PRETERITE-3PL"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 16,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "hablaron espanol y tuvieron tiempo",
                "hablaron espanol, tuvieron tiempo"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "Two families, one sentence.",
                "incorrect": "Hablaron espanol y tuvieron tiempo."
              }
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C55-sintesis-preterito-completo-we",
              "prompt": "Say: we ate at home.",
              "assesses": [
